  "kernelProfileBtfHint": "The kernel must carry BTF info; third-party ROMs and older devices may lack the struct offsets",
  "kernelProfilePasteExample": "Paste example",
  "kernelProfileWhyBtfTitle": "Why is BTF required?",
  "kernelProfileWhyBtfBody": "The generated profile forges credentials by writing to byte offsets inside struct cred, and those offsets change across kernel versions, so they cannot be hard-coded.\n\nIf the kernel image carries BTF (CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF), the real layout of task_struct and cred can be read straight from the image. Without BTF, task_cred, task_struct_size and cred_uid cannot be obtained and the profile cannot be generated.\n\nThe link must also support HTTP Range (partial download); otherwise the boot partition cannot be fetched on its own. Vendor OTA images and GKI devices such as Pixel usually satisfy both.",
