  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateTitle": "KASLR offset solving failed: no trustworthy kernel base address among the candidates",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateCause1": "Kernel just finished an OTA / just rebooted; the runtime layout no longer matches the profile assumptions",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateCause2": "The imported profile does not match the current kernel (boot.img version mismatch)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateCause3": "Abnormal background load polluted the k_itimer samples",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateCause4": "The tracefs sampling window caught no k_itimer records (SELinux blocking / insufficient Shizuku permission / too low background load)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateSuggestion1": "Reboot the device and try once more",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateSuggestion2": "Make sure the profile matches the current kernel version (see the kernel version on the device info row)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoSlideCandidateSuggestion3": "If it keeps failing, save the run log for investigation",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoKitimerRecordsTitle": "KASLR offset solving failed: the multi-size probe collected no k_itimer allocation records",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoKitimerRecordsCause1": "The tracefs kmem_cache_alloc event was never enabled (blocked by SELinux, or abnormal Shizuku authorization / mount)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoKitimerRecordsCause2": "The local k_itimer struct size is outside the candidate set 0x108 / 0x100 / 0x110 / 0x118, so no size matched",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoKitimerRecordsCause3": "System load was too low during sampling, so timer call sites were not triggered enough",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoKitimerRecordsSuggestion1": "Confirm Shizuku is authorized and tracefs is writable (Settings → Developer options)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoKitimerRecordsSuggestion2": "Reboot and retry so that sampling completes within a single boot",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibANoKitimerRecordsSuggestion3": "If it still fails, save the run log (including [calib_a] and arm_kmem_cache_alloc lines) for investigation",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibATracefsUnusableTitle": "tracefs unavailable: mounting / reading kernel trace events failed",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibATracefsUnusableCause1": "The SELinux policy blocked writes to tracefs",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibATracefsUnusableCause2": "Shizuku authorization problem (not started, or the permission was revoked)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibATracefsUnusableCause3": "Some ROMs strip the tracefs nodes",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibATracefsUnusableSuggestion1": "Confirm Shizuku is running and has granted permission to this app",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibATracefsUnusableSuggestion2": "Check whether USB debugging (wireless debugging) is available in Developer options",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibATracefsUnusableSuggestion3": "Restart Shizuku and retry; if it still fails, save the log for investigation",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBNoMatchingRecordsTitle": "Page offset solving failed: the base address from calibration A does not match reality",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBNoMatchingRecordsCause1": "The KASLR slide from calibration A is wrong (an upstream error; fix calibration A first)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBNoMatchingRecordsCause2": "Kernel memory layout changed between the two calibrations",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBNoMatchingRecordsSuggestion1": "Reboot so both calibrations complete within the same boot session",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBNoMatchingRecordsSuggestion2": "Re-run the full pipeline (do not skip the calibration steps)",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBInsufficientSamplesTitle": "Insufficient samples: too few triggered samples to solve the page offset",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBInsufficientSamplesCause1": "Background load was too low, so timer call sites were not triggered enough",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBInsufficientSamplesCause2": "The device just cold-booted and runtime services are not up yet",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBInsufficientSamplesSuggestion1": "Put the device under light use (e.g. play music) and retry",
  "ghostKeyDiagCalibBInsufficientSamplesSuggestion2": "Just run it again; samples are usually more plentiful the second time",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectResidualProcessTitle": "A leftover process from the previous round is still pinning a freed page; injecting again would crash the kernel",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectResidualProcessCause1": "The previous round never reached cleanup (force-quit / power loss)",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectResidualProcessSuggestion1": "You must reboot before retrying (killing the leftover process does not help)",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectRootdNotReadyTitle": "The exploit triggered but the root channel was never established: rootd timed out",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectRootdNotReadyCause1": "The device kernel carries a partial backport of the fix, making the UAF window unstable",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectRootdNotReadyCause2": "System load skewed the race timing",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectRootdNotReadySuggestion1": "Reboot and try once or twice more",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectRootdNotReadySuggestion2": "If it times out at the same point every time, the kernel may already be fixed; record the model and kernel version for feedback",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectOffsetTableMissingTitle": "Kernel offset table not loaded: injection has no profile data",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectOffsetTableMissingCause1": "No profile was imported, or the imported profile file is corrupt",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectOffsetTableMissingCause2": "The profile does not match the current kernel and was rejected by the engine",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectOffsetTableMissingSuggestion1": "Re-import a profile for this kernel version (extracted from boot.img)",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectTaskLeakFailedTitle": "task_struct address leak failed: no matching task_struct slab allocation in the scan window",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectTaskLeakFailedCause1": "The task_struct cache size disagrees with sizeof(task_struct) from BTF: the cache is created via kmem_cache_create_usercopy(\"task_struct\", arch_task_struct_size, 0x40, ...), where arch_task_struct_size is a runtime variable that vendors may extend via android_arch_task_struct_size= (up to 0x400)",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectTaskLeakFailedCause2": "The kmem_cache_alloc event was never enabled (tracefs not writable / SELinux denied)",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectTaskLeakFailedCause3": "A fork landed on a CPU that was not read (scanning covers all real cores, so this should not happen)",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectTaskLeakFailedSuggestion1": "Reboot the device and try again",
  "ghostKeyDiagInjectTaskLeakFailedSuggestion2": "In the log, [task] raw=0 means the event was not enabled; raw>0 with hits=0 means the size window is wrong — save the [task] sizes= line for investigation",
  "ghostKeyDiagVerifyFailedTitle": "Temporary root verification failed: the su check did not pass after the escalation channel came up",
  "ghostKeyDiagVerifyFailedCause1": "The credential rewrite during injection was incomplete (the upstream race only partly succeeded)",
  "ghostKeyDiagVerifyFailedCause2": "The verification subprocess was blocked by SELinux or a system policy",
  "ghostKeyDiagVerifyFailedSuggestion1": "Reboot and re-run the full pipeline",
  "ghostKeyDiagVerifyFailedSuggestion2": "Check the SELinux state (Settings → Developer options); do not force it to Permissive",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuAlreadyLiveTitle": "The kernel module is already resident: the old module is still in memory, so late-load was skipped",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuAlreadyLiveCause1": "The kernel module injected by the previous escalation is still alive",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuAlreadyLiveSuggestion1": "Reboot and run again so the manager can see the new takeover",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuAlreadyLiveSuggestion2": "If you only want root, there is no need to re-run — you already have temporary root",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuModuleAbsentTitle": "KSU late-load failed: the module never appeared in /proc/modules",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuModuleAbsentCause1": "The root manager / ksud on the device is too old, so the KMI does not match",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuModuleAbsentCause2": "The kernel restricted the module load path",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuModuleAbsentSuggestion1": "Update the root manager on the device to the latest version",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuModuleAbsentSuggestion2": "Retry once; if it keeps failing, save the log and note the manager version",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuKsudMissingTitle": "ksud not found: the selected root manager has no usable ksud",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuKsudMissingCause1": "No root manager is installed, or none is selected in the capsule",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuKsudMissingCause2": "That manager's ksud is incompatible with this architecture, or its library is corrupted",
  "ghostKeyDiagKsuKsudMissingSuggestion1": "Install a root manager, select it in the top-right capsule, then re-run the pipeline",
  "ghostKeyDiagHostShizukuUnavailableTitle": "Shizuku environment problem: the host process cannot start the escalation pipeline",
  "ghostKeyDiagHostShizukuUnavailableCause1": "The Shizuku service is not running (wireless debugging off or adb not connected)",
  "ghostKeyDiagHostShizukuUnavailableCause2": "The user denied the Shizuku authorization for this app",
  "ghostKeyDiagHostShizukuUnavailableSuggestion1": "Open the Shizuku app and make sure the service runs (either wireless debugging or adb)",
  "ghostKeyDiagHostShizukuUnavailableSuggestion2": "Request authorization again inside this app and allow it",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Title": "Pipeline terminated (exit=2): KASLR offset solving failed and no known sub-pattern matched",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Cause1": "Calibration A could not derive a trustworthy kernel base from k_itimer samples (the most common failure point)",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Cause2": "The current kernel layout disagrees with the selected profile (recent OTA / reboot, or a mismatched profile version, gives wrong timer_link/cred_link offsets)",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Cause3": "tracefs sampling was interrupted by an environment problem (SELinux blocking / Shizuku authorization lost / abnormal system load)",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Cause4": "Or this failure is a new variant not yet covered by the diagnoser (exit code 2 but the log string matched no rule)",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Suggestion1": "Reboot and retry once — KASLR differs on every boot, so a re-run usually solves it",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Suggestion2": "Make sure you are on the latest build (1.1.5) and the profile was extracted from the device boot.img with a release exactly matching the current kernel",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackExit2Suggestion3": "Do not just retry: save the full contents of the Run Log page (especially lines containing [calib_a] / [calib_b]) to help locate kernel compatibility issues",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackGenericTitle": "Pipeline terminated (exit={exit}): no known failure pattern matched",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackGenericCause1": "The timing-sensitive race window was missed, or the environment failed temporarily",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackGenericSuggestion1": "Do not just retry: copy and save the full contents of the Run Log page to help locate kernel compatibility issues",
  "ghostKeyDiagFallbackGenericSuggestion2": "After repeated failures, reboot and retry; if it still fails, save the run log for investigation",
